      "title": "I've won 5 hackathons and never taken a sales class. Turns…",
      "excerpt": "out they're the same skill. A hackathon is 24 hours to make a stranger care about something that didn't exist yesterday. So is a cold email. Both reward the exact same move: cut everything that isn't the point, lead with what they'd actually care about, and earn the next ten seconds before you try to earn the next ten minutes. The demo that wins isn't the one with the most features. The email that gets a reply isn't the one with the most words. Selling is just demoing to one person. P.S. throwb…",
